# Go
collector/bin/
collector/coverage.out

# Runtime caches (collector writes cables, recordings, etc. here).
# Bundled plugin assets must not live under any directory named data/;
# that pattern is recursive and hid naturalearth's go:embed extract after #11.
# Keep extracts beside their Go package (see naturalearth/regions.json).
data/
collector/data/
*.log

# Unreal Engine
unreal/.vs/
unreal/Binaries/
unreal/DerivedDataCache/
unreal/Intermediate/
unreal/Saved/
unreal/Plugins/*/Binaries/
unreal/Plugins/*/Intermediate/
*.sln

# Editors / OS
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.idea/
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Packaged builds
dist/

# Cached raw and converted NASA downloads (tools/fetch-earth-textures.py
# rebuilds all of it; the day/night textures alone can be several hundred MB
# at full resolution and must never enter the repository). Only the hand
# written attribution file in this directory is tracked.
unreal/SourceAssets/NASA/*.jpg
unreal/SourceAssets/NASA/*.png
unreal/SourceAssets/NASA/*.exr
unreal/SourceAssets/NASA/*.tif

# Personal collector setup (callsign, home QTH) - never published
collector/configs/local.json

# Generated textures: create_material_instances.py re-imports every texture
# on each editor start (import_texture always deletes and re-creates the
# asset), so tracked copies sat modified after every session. Every file in
# this folder is produced by that script from fetched or generated sources,
# and the Earth day/night textures are unlike every other Content/*.uasset:
# at 21600x10800 / 13500x6750 they compile to ~165 MB / ~31 MB. They are
# reproducible via tools/fetch-earth-textures.py + tools/run-editor.ps1 and,
# like the NASA source images, stay out of the repository. The
# tools/check-generated-assets.ps1 preflight makes tools/package.ps1 refuse to
# cook when any are missing.
unreal/Content/ION/Textures/

# Scratch levels: create_material_instances.py and generate_globe_mesh.py
# open them via open_empty_rebuild_level() and delete them again via
# discard_rebuild_level() (unreal/Scripts/_ion_common.py) on every run, so a
# tracked copy shows up as a deletion after every editor session. They are
# regenerated on demand.
unreal/Content/ION/Maps/L_Transient*.umap

# Local build/test/probe output at the repository root.
/.test-*.txt
/.package-out.txt

# Generated materials: create_material_instances.py rebuilds every master
# material and instance from scratch on each editor start (tools/run-editor.ps1),
# so tracked copies sat modified after every session. They are build output;
# tools/check-generated-assets.ps1 makes tools/package.ps1 refuse to cook when
# any are missing. Every file in this folder is produced by that script.
unreal/Content/ION/Materials/
